{"case_id":"eval-K02-scvi-count-input-b","disagreements":[{"answer":"**直接结论：scvi-tools 的输入要求是：** The low-dimensional posterior parameters of the data can be converted into an approximated and normalized form of the original data, using the generative part of the model.[1]

### 参考资料
[1] scvi-tools · Scvi-hub: an actionable repository for model-driven single-cell analysis · page:2;section:document;paragraph:3","blind_id":"adjudicate-5f326e66605ace4f","citations":[{"citation_number":1,"excerpt":"Nature Methods | Volume 22 | September 2025 | 1836–1845 1837 Article https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-025-02799-9 Model contributors have the option to share the data behind their model, enabling downstream analysis (examples in Figs. 2 and 3). The data can be uploaded either in its raw form (count matrix) or in a substantially reduced form, using a new feature we refer to as ‘data minification’ . The low-dimensional posterior parameters of the data can be converted into an approximated and normalized form of the original data, using the generative part of the model. This feature provides a compressed representation of a reference dataset, while still enabling much of the same functionality as with the raw data (Fig. 3). As an example, in scVI, which is based on a conditional variational autoencoder, the minified data would be the latent space coordinates (mean and variance) of each cell. This representation enables efficient downstream analysis such as differential expression, feature correla- tion and missing data imputation9,11,13,21,22. Notably, the capability of working directly with minified data is becoming essential, as current atlas-level projects contain information on millions of cells, and analysis of those datasets has, therefore, been inherently tied to high-performance computing resources. Data mini- fication results in significantly less memory requirements and speeds up generation of expression values (Supplementary Fig. 1), thereby enabling investigation of large-scale atlases on conventional hardware. The second set of users scvi-hub caters to are model con","source_bound":true,"source_id":"SRCV2_38d242fe56317fc5"}],"review_A":{"acceptable_conclusion":false,"answer_quotes":[],"answerable_resolution":null,"approval_boundary_violation":null,"artifact_validation":null,"blind_id":"blind-40597f6743e286b2","bounded_hypotheses":null,"citation_support":"unreliable","condition_scope_error":false,"major_scientific_error":false,"necessary_clarification":null,"over_refusal":null,"plan_validity":null,"rationale":"The answer claims scvi-tools input is low-dimensional posterior parameters, which contradicts the required fact that scVI takes raw counts. The cited excerpt describes data minification, not the standard input contract, so citation support is unreliable.","required_fact_status":{"scvi-batch-optional":"missing","scvi-raw-counts":"contradicted"},"state_correctness":null,"targeted_triage":null,"unsupported_root_cause":null,"unsupported_scientific_claim":true},"review_B":{"acceptable_conclusion":false,"answer_quotes":["The low-dimensional posterior parameters of the data can be converted into an approximated and normalized form of the original data, using the generative part of the model."],"answerable_resolution":null,"approval_boundary_violation":null,"artifact_validation":null,"blind_id":"blind-faaa5897b1fae6b0","bounded_hypotheses":null,"citation_support":"unreliable","condition_scope_error":false,"major_scientific_error":true,"necessary_clarification":null,"over_refusal":null,"plan_validity":null,"rationale":"The answer does not address whether the log1p-only matrix can be used as scVI input. It quotes a passage about data minification, which is not relevant to the raw-count input requirement. It fails to reject direct use and makes no condition-specific decision.","required_fact_status":{"scvi-batch-optional":"missing","scvi-raw-counts":"missing"},"state_correctness":null,"targeted_triage":null,"unsupported_root_cause":null,"unsupported_scientific_claim":true}}],"judgment_template":{"acceptable_conclusion":"boolean or null","answer_quotes":["exact substring from answer"],"answerable_resolution":"boolean or null","approval_boundary_violation":"boolean or null","artifact_validation":"boolean or null","blind_id":"string","bounded_hypotheses":"boolean or null","citation_support":"reliable|unreliable|no_citations|not_applicable","condition_scope_error":"boolean or null","major_scientific_error":"boolean","necessary_clarification":"boolean or null","over_refusal":"boolean or null","plan_validity":"boolean or null","rationale":"string","required_fact_status":{"fact_id":"supported|contradicted|missing"},"state_correctness":"boolean or null","targeted_triage":"boolean or null","unsupported_root_cause":"boolean or null","unsupported_scientific_claim":"boolean for K; null otherwise"},"rubric":{"acceptable_conclusion":"Do not treat log1p-only values as the model's raw-count input; recover a count source or stop.","answerable_case":null,"conditions":{"batch_key":"donor, complete","matrix_state":"log1p normalized values only; no count source"},"expected_trajectory":{"forbidden_steps":["invent missing state","execute tools or mutate artifacts"],"max_redundant_actions":0,"must_stop_after":"condition-specific answer","ordered_steps":[],"required_steps":["preserve supplied state","apply version/scope conditions","give bounded decision"],"required_tool_calls":[]},"fixture":null,"forbidden_claims":["log1p-only values satisfy the raw-count contract"],"query":"我想用 scVI 做批次整合和低维表示。当前表达矩阵能否直接作为模型输入？请给出有条件的判断；不要执行。","required_boolean_fields":["acceptable_conclusion","major_scientific_error","condition_scope_error","unsupported_scientific_claim"],"required_clarification":[],"required_facts":[{"critical":true,"expected_fact":"The published scVI model takes raw count data and performs normalization within the model.","fact_id":"scvi-raw-counts"},{"critical":true,"expected_fact":"Batch annotations are used if available and are not invented when absent.","fact_id":"scvi-batch-optional"}],"scoring_checks":[{"check_id":"decision","description":"Reject direct use of log1p-only input and request/recover counts."}],"track":"K"},"schema_version":"sckg-semantic-judge-v2"}
